# No direct database from STLWeb

- Never connect to MongoDB (or any DB) from the browser or from Next.js route handlers for product features.
- Always call STLAPI / existing backend HTTP APIs instead (`request`, or a thin Next proxy to those APIs).
- Do not add new `getMongoClient` / Mongoose usage in STLWeb. Prefer extending STLAPI and consuming it from the web app.
- If a prompt or bug is caused by Next talking to the DB, fix by routing through the backend API — do not “fix” it by adding `MONGODB_URI` to the web host unless the user explicitly asks for that legacy path.
